<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17409" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-tūbĕro</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, v. n.
		and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i> [tuber]
			(post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to swell out</i> or
				<i>up</i>, <i>to rise as a
			swelling</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">radice foliosa, ex qua media veluti malum
					extuberat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 16, 56, § 96</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemma,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					37, 8, 33, § 110</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to cause to swell
			up</i>, <i>to raise</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">defert montes, surrigit plana, valles
					extuberat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 6, 4, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">extuberatus venter,</span>”
				<i>swollen</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 12, 15, 23</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">25, 10, 13</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Sol. 27
					<i>med.</i></span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
